 Ref. 1 (2023)        DIST-AUG24 REV1-JUL24            20240830      2 1451
---- ENDF/B-VIII.1    MATERIAL    2         REVISION 1               2 1451
----- THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                                2 1451
------ ENDF-6                                                        2 1451
                                                                     2 1451
******************************************************************   2 1451
                                                                     2 1451
This evaluation is based on the methodology presented in [1].        2 1451
Path-integral molecular dynamics techniques have been used           2 1451
to produce the input for the neutron scattering model at the         2 1451
indicated temperatures. This includes the radial distribution and    2 1451
velocity autocorrelation functions, which were used to generate      2 1451
the static structure factor and the frequency spectrum. The static   2 1451
structure factor has been used to compute the coherent scattering    2 1451
function with the Skold approximation. For the dynamics, the         2 1451
frequency spectrum was decomposed into solid-like and diffusive      2 1451
parts, which were convoluted with vibrational and rotaional          2 1451
components using previously existing methods [2,3]. This formalism   2 1451
is coded in NJOY-H2D2 [4], which was used to generate the library.   2 1451
                                                                     2 1451
The approach has been benchmarked against previously existing        2 1451
libraries, theoretical calculations and available experimental       2 1451
data in [1].                                                         2 1451
                                                                     2 1451
 European Spallation Source ERIC                                     2 1451
                                                                     2 1451
